// Don't try to detect agents with client-side telemetry; bots mimic humans better every month.
// Instead, offer an economic bribe: machines want speed and structured data, humans want rendered UI.
function handle_incoming_session(request):
    // 1. Honor explicit delegation if the agent gains something by self-identifying
    if request.has_valid_delegation_token(): 
        session.type = AGENT_DECLARED
        suppress_ad_impressions() // Prevent ad fraud; an agent reading DOM is not human attention
        return serve_machine_optimized_payload(request, price_tier="standard")

    // 2. For unverified traffic, look for economic anomalies rather than browser fingerprinting
    signals = evaluate_interaction_physics(request) // e.g. parallel state queries, inhuman throughput
    if signals.is_synthetic_velocity:
        // Don't CAPTCHA or block; that kills the transaction if it's a real user's agent
        // Offer protocol negotiation: faster structured API in exchange for signed user consent token
        negotiation_response = offer_agent_handshake(request)
        if negotiation_response.accepted:
            session.type = AGENT_DISCLOSED
            return route_to_consent_aware_backend(negotiation_response)

    // 3. Fallback: treat ambiguous traffic as zero-attribution sandbox
    session.attribution_weight = 0.0 // Starve attribution models of contaminated touchpoints
    return serve_standard_web(request)

First sign a narrow claim—agent, principal, scope, and time;
Bind consent and touchpoint logs in one auditable chime.

Pilot it at trusted edges; label known and unknown;
Never call the rest “human” from an IP alone.

Let policy tiers decide what each signed caller may do;
Don’t price by shadow traits till law and proof come through.

Payments do not prove a gaze; spoofers can copy the tune;
We’ll publish error and revoke—the standard won’t come soon.
